# Codebase Context

## Tech Stack

See [README.md](mdc:README.md). We use `pnpm` as our package manager, with a pnpm workspace (`apps/*` + `packages/*`).

## Codebase Structure and Configuration

This repo is a monorepo. Apps are workspace packages deployed as subdomains:

- [+page.svelte](mdc:apps/main/src/routes/+page.svelte) — camball.io (`@camball/main`), the site home
- [+page.svelte](mdc:apps/blog/src/routes/+page.svelte) — blog.camball.io (`@camball/blog`), the blog site
- [+page.svelte](mdc:apps/archive/src/routes/+page.svelte) — archive.camball.io (`@camball/archive`), a showcase of Instagram videos embedded with the embed API
- [+page.svelte](mdc:apps/contact/src/routes/+page.svelte) — contact.camball.io (`@camball/contact`), a page for others to get in touch
- [+page.svelte](mdc:apps/resume/src/routes/+page.svelte) — resume.camball.io (`@camball/resume`), a resume of work

Shared UI lives in [`packages/ui`](mdc:packages/ui) as `@camball/ui` (workspace dependency). Apps import from `@camball/ui/...` and keep a standard per-app `$lib` (`src/lib`) for local code.

Shared package contents:

- CSS: [app.css](mdc:packages/ui/app.css)
- shadcn-svelte components under [components/](mdc:packages/ui/components) (see [index.ts](mdc:packages/ui/components/index.ts)). Install new ones with `npx shadcn-svelte@latest add <component>` (aliases point at `@camball/ui` via [components.json](mdc:components.json))
- Assets under [assets/](mdc:packages/ui/assets) — import via Vite, e.g., `import img from '@camball/ui/assets/example.png'`
- Utils: [utils.ts](mdc:packages/ui/utils.ts)

Also shared at the repo root: TypeScript config, Tailwind config, Vite/Vitest/Oxlint tooling. Each app has its own `package.json`, `svelte.config.js`, `tsconfig.json`, and `vite.config.ts`.

## Coding Practices and Style

- Use shadcn-svelte components, when applicable, before creating our own
- This repo uses Tailwind v4, not v3. This means that [tailwind.config.ts](mdc:tailwind.config.ts) is legacy and should not be updated unless absolutely necessary. Use Tailwind styles, and only create our own if absolutely necessary. If we need to create custom CSS for any reason or customise Tailwind, configuration should go in [app.css](mdc:packages/ui/app.css), unless it is specific to only a single app, in which case it should go in that app's `src/app.css`.
- Ensure Svelte 5 syntax is used (no Svelte 4).
- Shared images live in `@camball/ui/assets` and should be imported (not referenced as `$lib/assets/...` strings).
- The whole site supports dark and light mode. Usually this can be handled by specifying the `dark:` variant in Tailwind, but if the theme needs to be used explicitly, it can be done with `import { mode } from 'mode-watcher';`, then checking like `{#if mode.current === 'dark'}`.
